{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>A calf, a son of cattle.</b> During the seven days of ordination there was a bull for a sin-offering and also a ram for a burnt-offering, and he did not mention together with 'a calf, a son of cattle' whether it is a yearling. And what seems likely to me is that 'bull' is like 'calf,' without [specifying] a year." "<b>Without blemish.</b> Upon the calf and upon the ram. And the offering of ordination was to decontaminate the altar, while this calf was to make atonement for Aaron. And I have already explained this word."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The phrase 'a son of cattle' translates בן בקר literally; Ibn Ezra is discussing why the age specification 'son of a year' (בן שנה) found elsewhere is absent here."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:10.507803614Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}